{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0418c7aa98cb910ad8bed9a8fcdd37b47eea038ce0ddcbd03117eae3a3be5e78"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI accepts --model (e.g. llamacpp/qwen3.6-35b-a3b, anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5, ollama/qwen3.5, lmstudio/local-model) and --list-models; bare invocation launches the models.json default."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2f12b6a0e142666a8b84ea075846375078058067bf2b5955072552beba339218"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Model overrides resolve from LITTLE_CODER_MODELS_FILE, XDG config, or ~/.config/little-coder/models.json, with provider-level full replacement rather than deep merge; base-URL env vars take precedence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4dec468a368c8cbe8d00d7d944e7378854cde64591c15b1bd8039f54920e9fd4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"little-coder is built on pi as a plain dependency, adding roughly 30 extensions, 30 skill markdown files, and a Python benchmark harness under .pi/extensions/, skills/, and benchmarks/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_571802fdf1548175cb5390dbb2a94c0d4733ad8a71d05a1b585d47718cc9d18d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Node.js 22.19+; installable via a curl script, npm install -g, or bun, and the launcher is a Node script so Node must remain on PATH even when installed with bun."},{"claim_ids":["clm_649ede035a5382d279aabbe58ef0c8fd1bc9447aea1ea2316ee7b2bc97dc2c06"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Background jobs outlive a turn but not the session: they run in their own process group, are reaped on shutdown, and carry a watchdog that kills the group if little-coder's pid disappears."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b70715448dfe412c78f18c59a299169b75c1402dec1d394187c1a417e64abf0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every command in a chain is judged individually, and any shell write via redirects, tee, or dd of= is refused; LITTLE_CODER_PERMISSION_MODE offers auto, accept-all, and manual modes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6eae57985efec0d87f8f20521e37212c48ba33a2d01ee70da2f97fa684fe0da5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Published results include Aider Polyglot 45.56% (Qwen3.5-9B) and 78.67% (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), Terminal-Bench-Core 40.0%, Terminal-Bench 2.0 leaderboard 24.6%±3.2, and GAIA validation 40.00%, all on an 8 GB VRAM laptop with no cloud inference."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d30a390208c87bd250b0333f8b31fa608e9950bc43de6c550de6fd49190c835"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can opt into extra extensions via ~/.config/little-coder/extensions/, the LITTLE_CODER_EXTRA_EXTENSIONS variable, or a --with-pi-extensions relaunch; /extensions shows what loaded."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a77b998a9e8b61909a17fa87a3daf1382d8639e325a8fd2201dfc8f2863de9c5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ShellStart runs background jobs with wake_on triggers (exit, regex match, silence, every_n_matches), delivering bounded excerpts plus exit code, with ShellLog, ShellList, ShellSend, and ShellStop companions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b5a3c515f240c1b00522d67550c23f6c786bfb8c675f46126fd461653aaa01ad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Deep Research (f2 or /deep-research) fans out read-only sub-coders in an ephemeral scratch directory and returns one cited markdown report saved near the working directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d348bdaaf8e1252b4a40fc5a72530dedfd8a4bb573100306a6f25ba387f9e63d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per-phase model selection lets planning and implementation use different models via /plan-model, /action-model, and /model-handover auto|manual, with handover deferred until implementation begins."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d55d4e929c27f7aeb1c5d0a5a2dc62f8f4d5c1940e6cb80616cd2084af09eb16"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plan Mode (ctrl+q or --plan-mode) researches with sub-coders, asks 1-3 clarifying questions, writes a plan, and /implement starts a fresh session on the action model; Esc cancels."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e4ef3b41caa47b7d58c732c03f9b6383daf3ea49d75972dce7d45f25184e27b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Without a vision projector (mmproj) on the llama.cpp server, image attachments are rejected with a 4xx, though text-only use still works."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e5dc8582abf328cc8f7666f6585d4704f093d9c7cc0cb6611d31726d874e4172"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets coding agents for small local models on consumer laptops, with Phase 2 focused on operating large, messy markdown knowledge bases token-efficiently."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e91dc5eae3390e0b09056f77d137ac6333d38a0517c8ef6cbbaab84095a5d865"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Shell calls are gated against a built-in safe-prefix whitelist before pi's confirmation flow; rm and sudo are excluded, and LITTLE_CODER_BASH_ALLOW adds prefixes per deployment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa946be99f49e15972e8f99e58c2d792cb0da95917c4b25019266369dd2f55b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A compaction watchdog checks context at every turn boundary and triggers pi's compaction at 80% of the window, tunable via LITTLE_CODER_COMPACT_AT_PERCENT, and pauses automatic compaction if a pass frees too little."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fe7a4ac89485c78a31919f0da9600f40d78c2026c0dd63664e0a09de80a16014"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The launcher runs pi with --no-extensions and wires in only the bundled set, keeping cold-start context near 7k tokens and making loaded behavior fixed at ship time."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0418c7aa98cb910ad8bed9a8fcdd37b47eea038ce0ddcbd03117eae3a3be5e78","clm_2f12b6a0e142666a8b84ea075846375078058067bf2b5955072552beba339218","clm_4dec468a368c8cbe8d00d7d944e7378854cde64591c15b1bd8039f54920e9fd4","clm_571802fdf1548175cb5390dbb2a94c0d4733ad8a71d05a1b585d47718cc9d18d","clm_649ede035a5382d279aabbe58ef0c8fd1bc9447aea1ea2316ee7b2bc97dc2c06","clm_6b70715448dfe412c78f18c59a299169b75c1402dec1d394187c1a417e64abf0","clm_6eae57985efec0d87f8f20521e37212c48ba33a2d01ee70da2f97fa684fe0da5","clm_9d30a390208c87bd250b0333f8b31fa608e9950bc43de6c550de6fd49190c835","clm_a77b998a9e8b61909a17fa87a3daf1382d8639e325a8fd2201dfc8f2863de9c5","clm_b5a3c515f240c1b00522d67550c23f6c786bfb8c675f46126fd461653aaa01ad","clm_d348bdaaf8e1252b4a40fc5a72530dedfd8a4bb573100306a6f25ba387f9e63d","clm_d55d4e929c27f7aeb1c5d0a5a2dc62f8f4d5c1940e6cb80616cd2084af09eb16","clm_e4ef3b41caa47b7d58c732c03f9b6383daf3ea49d75972dce7d45f25184e27b7","clm_e5dc8582abf328cc8f7666f6585d4704f093d9c7cc0cb6611d31726d874e4172","clm_e91dc5eae3390e0b09056f77d137ac6333d38a0517c8ef6cbbaab84095a5d865","clm_fa946be99f49e15972e8f99e58c2d792cb0da95917c4b25019266369dd2f55b8","clm_fe7a4ac89485c78a31919f0da9600f40d78c2026c0dd63664e0a09de80a16014"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:05:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_fa984a64620448b9b9202de0fc593dad","id":"pg_e1c4e52238ca56f78816b20013a64c04","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/itayinbarr-little-coder-readme-md-a9e467f2be43-b20013a64c04.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c1b1b23c37b75283a09e43706b413d49"],"title":"itayinbarr/little-coder/README.md @ a9e467f2be43","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:05:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fa984a64620448b9b9202de0fc593dad"}
